{"uid":"e0ceb508df54c706","name":"test_ui_log_endpoint_matches_cli_pretty_rendering","fullName":"tests.test_cli_ui#test_ui_log_endpoint_matches_cli_pretty_rendering","historyId":"eae0f877d5765456b282cee8dd134e91","time":{"start":1792160666285,"stop":1792160668651,"duration":2366},"description":"Task 014: the hub's `/api/runs/<id>/logs` endpoint must render\n    through the EXACT SAME `log_render.render_to_lines` function\n    `ralphctl logs` uses -- so this asserts the endpoint's `lines` list,\n    joined with newlines, is byte-for-byte identical to what `ralphctl logs\n    <id> --tail 0` prints, driven in-process (task 004, requirement F) so\n    only the process BOUNDARY moved -- the rendering stays non-TTY exactly\n    as a piped subprocess's stdout would be (this endpoint's own\n    `tty=False` rendering), modulo the CLI's own trailing\n    newline, which `logs` prints and a list-of-lines representation has\n    no equivalent slot for.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 014: the hub's <code>/api/runs/&lt;id&gt;/logs</code> endpoint must render<br />\nthrough the EXACT SAME <code>log_render.render_to_lines</code> function<br />\n<code>ralphctl logs</code> uses -- so this asserts the endpoint's <code>lines</code> list,<br />\njoined with newlines, is byte-for-byte identical to what <code>ralphctl logs &lt;id&gt; --tail 0</code> prints, driven in-process (task 004, requirement F) so<br />\nonly the process BOUNDARY moved -- the rendering stays non-TTY exactly<br />\nas a piped subprocess's stdout would be (this endpoint's own<br />\n<code>tty=False</code> rendering), modulo the CLI's own trailing<br />\nnewline, which <code>logs</code> prints and a list-of-lines representation has<br />\nno equivalent slot for.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1792160405908,"stop":1792160405908,"duration":0},"status":"passed",